{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-161276" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the triple integral \n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}\\frac{z{sec}^{2}⁡x}{y}\\,\\text{d}V\n$$\n\nover the box $R={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,-\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\le x\\le \\frac{\\pi }{3},\\,{e}^{2}\\le y\\le {e}^{5},\\,0\\le z\\le 4}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069983/state.json" "file_sha256" "1a1376ef5e7ff84d9af3a45325974d4601f5250370f1f40cce9b3e347b15d675"} {"question" "q-161276" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we express our triple integral as a repeated integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∭}_{R}\\frac{z{sec}^{2}⁡x}{y}\\,\\text{d}V & ={\\int }_{0}^{4}{\\int }_{{e}^{2}}^{{e}^{5}}{\\int }_{-\\pi /4}^{\\pi /3}\\frac{z{sec}^{2}⁡x}{y}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}z\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the domain of integration $R=[-\\frac{\\pi }{4},\\frac{\\pi }{3}]\\times [{e}^{2},{e}^{5}]\\times [0,4]$ is a rectangular box, and the integrand can be expressed as $f(x)\\cdot g(y)\\cdot h(z),$ we can rewrite our repeated integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{4}{\\int }_{{e}^{2}}^{{e}^{5}}{\\int }_{-\\pi /4}^{\\pi /3}\\frac{z{sec}^{2}⁡x}{y}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}z & ={\\int }_{0}^{4}{\\int }_{{e}^{2}}^{{e}^{5}}{\\int }_{-\\pi /4}^{\\pi /3}{sec}^{2}⁡x\\cdot \\frac{1}{y}\\cdot z\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}z \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-\\pi /4}^{\\pi /3}{sec}^{2}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x{\\int }_{{e}^{2}}^{{e}^{5}}\\frac{1}{y}\\,\\text{d}y{\\int }_{0}^{4}z\\,\\text{d}z\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEvaluating each integral separately, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-\\pi /4}^{\\pi /3}{sec}^{2}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x{\\int }_{{e}^{2}}^{{e}^{5}}\\frac{1}{y}\\,\\text{d}y{\\int }_{0}^{4}z\\,\\text{d}z & =[\\operatorname{tan}⁡x]_{-\\pi /4}^{\\pi /3}\\cdot [\\operatorname{ln}⁡y]_{{e}^{2}}^{{e}^{5}}\\cdot {[\\frac{{z}^{2}}{2}]}_{0}^{4} \\\\  & =(\\sqrt{3}+1)\\cdot (5-2)\\cdot (8-0) \\\\  & =(\\sqrt{3}+1)\\cdot 3\\cdot 8 \\\\  & =24(\\sqrt{3}+1).\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069983/state.json" "file_sha256" "1a1376ef5e7ff84d9af3a45325974d4601f5250370f1f40cce9b3e347b15d675"} {"question" "q-161276" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069983/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "50dedbc57f1439bee687044f6c6e9aced5d7aa3ed4482530a56b42c77db9519f"} {"question" "q-161276" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069983/state.json" "file_sha256" "1a1376ef5e7ff84d9af3a45325974d4601f5250370f1f40cce9b3e347b15d675"} {"question" "q-161276" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "12(\\sqrt{3}-1)"] ["math" "12\\sqrt{3}"] ["math" "24(\\sqrt{3}+1)"] ["math" "2\\sqrt{3}-1"] ["math" "4(\\sqrt{3}-1)"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069983/state.json" "file_sha256" "1a1376ef5e7ff84d9af3a45325974d4601f5250370f1f40cce9b3e347b15d675"} {"question" "q-161276" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "24(\\sqrt{3}+1)"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069983/state.json" "file_sha256" "1a1376ef5e7ff84d9af3a45325974d4601f5250370f1f40cce9b3e347b15d675"} {"question" "q-161279" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the triple integral \n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}\\frac{{3}^{y-1}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{z-4}\\,\\text{d}V\n$$\n\nover the box $R={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,\\frac{\\pi }{3}\\le x\\le \\frac{\\pi }{2},\\,0\\le y\\le 1,\\,5\\le z\\le 7}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069983/state.json" "file_sha256" "1a1376ef5e7ff84d9af3a45325974d4601f5250370f1f40cce9b3e347b15d675"} {"question" "q-161279" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we express our triple integral as a repeated integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∭}_{R}\\frac{{3}^{y-1}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{z-4}\\,\\text{d}V & ={\\int }_{5}^{7}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{\\pi /3}^{\\pi /2}\\frac{{3}^{y-1}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{z-4}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}z\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the domain of integration $R=[\\frac{\\pi }{3},\\frac{\\pi }{2}]\\times [0,1]\\times [5,7]$ is a rectangular box and the integrand can be expressed as $f(x)\\cdot g(y)\\cdot h(z),$ we can rewrite our repeated integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{5}^{7}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{\\pi /3}^{\\pi /2}\\frac{{3}^{y-1}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{z-4}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}z & ={\\int }_{5}^{7}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{\\pi /3}^{\\pi /2}\\frac{{3}^{y-1}\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{z-4}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}z \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /3}^{\\pi /2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x{\\int }_{0}^{1}{3}^{y-1}\\,\\text{d}y{\\int }_{5}^{7}\\frac{1}{z-4}\\,\\text{d}z\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEvaluating each integral separately, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{\\pi /3}^{\\pi /2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x{\\int }_{0}^{1}{3}^{y-1}\\,\\text{d}y{\\int }_{5}^{7}\\frac{1}{z-4}\\,\\text{d}z & =[-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x]_{\\pi /3}^{\\pi /2}\\cdot {[\\frac{{3}^{y-1}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}]}_{0}^{1}\\cdot [\\operatorname{ln}⁡(z-4)]_{5}^{7} \\\\  & =(-0+\\frac{1}{2})\\cdot (\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}-\\frac{1}{3\\operatorname{ln}⁡3})\\cdot (\\operatorname{ln}⁡3-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot \\frac{2}{3\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}\\cdot \\operatorname{ln}⁡3 \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069983/state.json" "file_sha256" "1a1376ef5e7ff84d9af3a45325974d4601f5250370f1f40cce9b3e347b15d675"} {"question" "q-161279" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069983/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "50dedbc57f1439bee687044f6c6e9aced5d7aa3ed4482530a56b42c77db9519f"} {"question" "q-161279" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069983/state.json" "file_sha256" "1a1376ef5e7ff84d9af3a45325974d4601f5250370f1f40cce9b3e347b15d675"} {"question" "q-161279" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "3"] ["math" "3\\operatorname{ln}⁡3"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{3}"] ["math" "\\frac{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3-3}"] ["math" "\\frac{2}{3\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069983/state.json" "file_sha256" "1a1376ef5e7ff84d9af3a45325974d4601f5250370f1f40cce9b3e347b15d675"} {"question" "q-161279" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{3}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069983/state.json" "file_sha256" "1a1376ef5e7ff84d9af3a45325974d4601f5250370f1f40cce9b3e347b15d675"} {"question" "q-161369" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "By integrating first with respect to $y,$ then $x,$ and then $z,$ evaluate the triple integral \n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}{x}^{2}z+\\frac{1}{y}\\,dV\n$$\n\nover the rectangular box $R={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 2,\\,1\\le y\\le 3,\\,-1\\le z\\le 1}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069983/state.json" "file_sha256" "1a1376ef5e7ff84d9af3a45325974d4601f5250370f1f40cce9b3e347b15d675"} {"question" "q-161369" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we express our triple integral as a repeated integral:\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}{x}^{2}z+\\frac{1}{y}\\,\\text{d}V={\\int }_{-1}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{1}^{3}{x}^{2}z+\\frac{1}{y}\\,dy\\,dx\\,dz\n$$\n\nSince we're integrating first with respect to $y,$ then $x,$ and then $z,$ we write $\\text{d}V=\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}z.$\n\nFirst, we evaluate the inner integral with respect to $y,$ treating $x$ and $z$ as constants: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-1}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{1}^{3}{x}^{2}z+\\frac{1}{y}\\,dy\\,dx\\,dz & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{2}[{\\int }_{1}^{3}{x}^{2}z+\\frac{1}{y}\\,dy]dx\\,dz \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{2}[{x}^{2}zy+\\operatorname{ln}⁡|y|]_{y=1}^{y=3}\\,dx\\,dz \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{x}^{2}z(3-1)+(\\operatorname{ln}⁡3-0)\\,dx\\,dz \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{2}2{x}^{2}z+\\operatorname{ln}⁡3\\,dx\\,dz\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate the inner integral with respect to $x,$ treating $z$ as a constant: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-1}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{2}2{x}^{2}z+\\operatorname{ln}⁡3\\,dx\\,dz & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}[{\\int }_{0}^{2}2z{x}^{2}+\\operatorname{ln}⁡3\\,dx]dz \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}{[\\frac{2}{3}\\,z{x}^{3}+x\\operatorname{ln}⁡3]}_{x=0}^{x=2}\\,dz \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}\\frac{2}{3}\\,z(8-0)+(2-0)\\operatorname{ln}⁡3\\,dz \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}\\frac{16}{3}\\,z+2\\operatorname{ln}⁡3\\,dz\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we integrate with respect to $z:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-1}^{1}\\frac{16}{3}z+2\\operatorname{ln}⁡3\\,dz & ={[\\frac{8}{3}{z}^{2}+2z\\operatorname{ln}⁡3]}_{z=-1}^{z=1} \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{3}(1-1)+2(1-(-1))\\operatorname{ln}⁡3 \\\\  & =4\\operatorname{ln}⁡3\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069983/state.json" "file_sha256" "1a1376ef5e7ff84d9af3a45325974d4601f5250370f1f40cce9b3e347b15d675"} {"question" "q-161369" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069983/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "50dedbc57f1439bee687044f6c6e9aced5d7aa3ed4482530a56b42c77db9519f"} {"question" "q-161369" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069983/state.json" "file_sha256" "1a1376ef5e7ff84d9af3a45325974d4601f5250370f1f40cce9b3e347b15d675"} {"question" "q-161369" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "2-\\operatorname{ln}⁡3"] ["math" "2\\operatorname{ln}⁡3"] ["math" "3-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡2"] ["math" "3\\operatorname{ln}⁡2"] ["math" "4\\operatorname{ln}⁡3"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069983/state.json" "file_sha256" "1a1376ef5e7ff84d9af3a45325974d4601f5250370f1f40cce9b3e347b15d675"} {"question" "q-161369" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "4\\operatorname{ln}⁡3"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069983/state.json" "file_sha256" "1a1376ef5e7ff84d9af3a45325974d4601f5250370f1f40cce9b3e347b15d675"} {"question" "q-161371" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "By integrating first with respect to $y,$ then $z,$ and then $x,$ evaluate the triple integral \n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+y+z)\\,dV\n$$\n\nover the rectangular box $R={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le \\frac{\\pi }{2},\\,0\\le y\\le \\pi ,\\,0\\le z\\le \\pi }.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069983/state.json" "file_sha256" "1a1376ef5e7ff84d9af3a45325974d4601f5250370f1f40cce9b3e347b15d675"} {"question" "q-161371" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we express our triple integral as a repeated integral:\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+y+z)\\,\\text{d}V={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+y+z)\\,dy\\,dz\\,dx\n$$\n\nSince we're integrating first with respect to $y,$ then $z,$ and then $x,$ we write $\\text{d}V=\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}x.$\n\nFirst, we evaluate the inner integral with respect to $y,$ treating $x$ and $z$ as constants: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+y+z)\\,dy\\,dz\\,dx & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }[{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+y+z)\\,dy]dz\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }[-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x+y+z)]_{0}^{\\pi }\\,dz\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x+z+\\pi )+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x+z+0)\\,dz\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x+z)+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x+z)\\,dz\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x+z)\\,dz\\,dx\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate the inner integral with respect to $z,$ treating $x$ as a constant: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x+z)\\,dz\\,dx & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}[{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x+z)\\,dz]dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}2[\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+z)]_{z=0}^{z=\\pi }\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}2(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+\\pi )-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+0))\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}2(-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)\\,dx \\\\  & =-4{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,dx\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we integrate with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-4{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,dx & =4[\\operatorname{cos}⁡x]_{x=0}^{x=\\pi /2} \\\\  & =4(0-1) \\\\  & =-4\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069983/state.json" "file_sha256" "1a1376ef5e7ff84d9af3a45325974d4601f5250370f1f40cce9b3e347b15d675"} {"question" "q-161371" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069983/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "50dedbc57f1439bee687044f6c6e9aced5d7aa3ed4482530a56b42c77db9519f"} {"question" "q-161371" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069983/state.json" "file_sha256" "1a1376ef5e7ff84d9af3a45325974d4601f5250370f1f40cce9b3e347b15d675"} {"question" "q-161371" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-4"] ["math" "-8"] ["math" "1"] ["math" "2"] ["math" "6"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069983/state.json" "file_sha256" "1a1376ef5e7ff84d9af3a45325974d4601f5250370f1f40cce9b3e347b15d675"} {"question" "q-161371" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-4"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069983/state.json" "file_sha256" "1a1376ef5e7ff84d9af3a45325974d4601f5250370f1f40cce9b3e347b15d675"} {"question" "q-161373" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "By integrating first with respect to $x,$ then $y,$ and then $z,$ evaluate the triple integral \n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}2x+3{y}^{2}+4{z}^{3}\\,dV\n$$\n\nover the rectangular box $R={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 3,\\,0\\le y\\le 2,\\,0\\le z\\le 1}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069983/state.json" "file_sha256" "1a1376ef5e7ff84d9af3a45325974d4601f5250370f1f40cce9b3e347b15d675"} {"question" "q-161373" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we express our triple integral as a repeated integral:\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}2x+3{y}^{2}+4{z}^{3}\\,\\text{d}V={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{3}2x+3{y}^{2}+4{z}^{3}\\,dx\\,dy\\,dz\n$$\n\nSince we're integrating first with respect to $x,$ then $y,$ and then $z,$ we write $\\text{d}V=\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}z.$\n\nFirst, we evaluate the inner integral with respect to $x,$ treating $y$ and $z$ as constants: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{3}2x+3{y}^{2}+4{z}^{3}\\,dx\\,dy\\,dz & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{2}[{\\int }_{0}^{3}2x+3{y}^{2}+4{z}^{3}\\,dx]dy\\,dz \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{2}[{x}^{2}+(3{y}^{2}+4{z}^{3})x]_{x=0}^{x=3}\\,dy\\,dz \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{2}(9-0)+(3{y}^{2}+4{z}^{3})(3-0)\\,dy\\,dz \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{2}9+9{y}^{2}+12{z}^{3}\\,dy\\,dz\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate the inner integral with respect to $y,$ treating $z$ as a constant: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{2}9+9{y}^{2}+12{z}^{3}\\,dy\\,dz & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}[{\\int }_{0}^{2}9+12{z}^{3}+9{y}^{2}\\,dy]dz \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}[(9+12{z}^{3})y+3{y}^{3}]_{y=0}^{y=2}\\,dz \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(9+12{z}^{3})(2-0)+3(8-0)\\,dz \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}18+24{z}^{3}+24\\,dz \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}42+24{z}^{3}\\,dz\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we integrate with respect to $z:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}42+24{z}^{3}\\,dz & =[42z+6{z}^{4}]_{z=0}^{z=1} \\\\  & =42(1-0)+6(1-0) \\\\  & =48\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069983/state.json" "file_sha256" "1a1376ef5e7ff84d9af3a45325974d4601f5250370f1f40cce9b3e347b15d675"} {"question" "q-161373" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069983/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "50dedbc57f1439bee687044f6c6e9aced5d7aa3ed4482530a56b42c77db9519f"} {"question" "q-161373" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069983/state.json" "file_sha256" "1a1376ef5e7ff84d9af3a45325974d4601f5250370f1f40cce9b3e347b15d675"} {"question" "q-161373" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "18"] ["math" "26"] ["math" "36"] ["math" "48"] ["math" "54"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069983/state.json" "file_sha256" "1a1376ef5e7ff84d9af3a45325974d4601f5250370f1f40cce9b3e347b15d675"} {"question" "q-161373" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "48"] "categor